# Sleep App — local environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in what you need. `.env.local` is
# gitignored; this template is checked in so a future clone knows what the
# project expects.
#
# The app itself no longer reads a single API key. The in-app story
# generator was removed on 2026-09-15 and the library ships as files in
# public/, so nothing in the browser bundle talks to ElevenLabs or Anthropic.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, VITE_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY and
# VITE_ELEVENLABS_USE_PROJECTS all went with it — delete them from your
# `.env.local`, since a `VITE_`-prefixed variable is exposed to client code
# and there is no longer any reason to hand one to the bundler.

# Dev server over TLS. Set to 1 and Vite terminates TLS itself, binding to
# all interfaces, so a phone on the same network can load the PWA (a service
# worker needs a secure context). See vite.config.ts.
VITE_USE_HTTPS=

# ── Desk-side tools only ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are read by Node scripts in tools/ (gen-story.ts, gen-meditation.ts)
# when rendering library content, never by the app. The two keys are
# deliberately NOT `VITE_`-prefixed so the bundler cannot pick them up.
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY     — writing story scripts
#   ELEVEN_LABS_API_KEY   — narration
#   VITE_VOICE_TIDE / _STONE / _GLEN — override the default voice ids.
#     These carry the prefix for historical reasons and are read from
#     process.env by the tools; they hold ids, not secrets.
